      "writtenOn": "2020-12-01T16:20:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The name is intentional actually. processXyzFromAgent is intended to be called only on information coming directly from the agent. Think of it as preprocessing the information it sends us. We have one for LinkProperties and one for NetworkCapabilities.\n\nmixInCapabilities, on the other hand, is called in a lot more places:\n\n - applyBackgroundChangeForRematch\n - registerNetworkAgentInternal\n - updateCapabilities\n   - handleLingerComplete\n   - EVENT_NETWORK_CAPABILITIES_CHANGED\n   - EVENT_UNDERLYING_NETWORKS_CHANGED\n   - EVENT_PROBE_STATUS_CHANGED\n   - EVENT_PROVISIONING_NOTIFICATION\n   - handleNetworkTested\n   - handleRemoveNetworkRequest\n   - propagateUnderlyingNetworkCapabilities\n\nI think this is because mixInCapabilities mixes the agent capabilities with the ConnectivityService/NetworkMonitor/...-derived capabilities, and thus needs to be called whenever the latter change (e.g., network validated, network goes into the background, etc.). I\u0027m not 100% sure these are all needed, but in any case, the two methods have different purposes.\n\nI do think the docstrings try to explain the difference: the docstring of processCapabilitiesFromAgent says \"stores into |nai|...\" and the docstring of mixInCapabilities says \"augments the NetworkCapabilities...\", so if someone is really paying attention, they\u0027ll notice that one modifies nai and one modifies NetworkCapabilities.\n\nBut I agree this is very difficult to understand. Suggestions on how to improve things welcome. One thing I can think of might be to move the check for losing immutable capabilities from mixInCapabilities to processCapabilitiesFromAgent, but that doesn\u0027t really make much things easier to understand.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "6546465b_0f7573e1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6354,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 6354,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "6aa06a33d7680345641854a865b0f5c3506afbc8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
